cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "acp-cockpit: a browser client for coding agents over the Agent Client Protocol"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: 2026-09-05
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Campolim
    given-names: Fabio
abstract: >
  A local, browser-based client for coding agents that speak the Agent
  Client Protocol (ACP). A small Python server spawns the agent's ACP
  adapter as a subprocess and renders the structured conversation -
  messages, thinking summaries, tool calls with diffs, plans - in tabbed
  browser sessions. Everything agent-specific is data in a profile, file
  access is confined to the project directory, approvals and the agent's
  own questions are explicit dialogs, and every protocol frame is
  recorded: what the protocol carries is shown, never silently dropped.
keywords:
  - agent-client-protocol
  - claude-code
  - coding-agents
  - tornado
  - developer-tools
